  "reply_to_user": "Hi Mei, thanks for reporting this. Your account is active, and your recent Microsoft 365 sign-ins have all succeeded, so the account itself is fine. Please try this on your Mac: in Excel, open the Excel menu (or File), choose Account, sign out, then quit all Office apps (Excel, Word, Outlook, PowerPoint). Reopen Excel and sign in with your brightline.example email address, not a personal Microsoft account. If the 'Unlicensed Product' banner is still there after that, reply to this ticket and we will escalate it to our second-level team to check your Office license assignment. Also, your mailbox is almost full (about 99% used), so please clear out some old email or large attachments when you can.",
  "internal_note": "Checked lookup_user: user 9 (Mei Chen, Operations), active, not locked, 0 failed logins, not blocked, no must-change-password. Sign-in logs for last 14 days: all m365 and vpn sign-ins succeeded with Duo push from Chicago on corporate/residential networks, no failures or hosting-network sign-ins. Device BL-LT-0109 is a macOS 15 laptop, online, last check-in 2026-10-11, 75 GB free (14.6%), no warnings. Nothing found that blocks activation. KB-026 escalation criteria (user signs in correctly and still sees Unlicensed product) are not yet met because the user has not yet tried the sign-out/sign-in step. KB-026 steps are Windows-specific; the Mac equivalent (Excel menu or File > Account > Sign Out) was given to the user. If still unlicensed after retry, escalate to Tier 2 to verify the M365 license assignment for user 9. Side note: mailbox is 50,890 of 51,200 MB (99.4%), which may cause sync or send problems and needs a separate cleanup or quota review.",
